+    // CFOP defense (Coroutine-Aware CFI): reserve a header slot for the
+    // per-type TypeID used by the dispatch-table CFI pass.  It sits at a FIXED
+    // offset 16 (right after the two header pointers) *before* the promise, so
+    // the TypeID offset is the same for every coroutine type regardless of
+    // promise size.  CoroEarly::lowerCoroPromise is updated to match: it now
+    // accounts for this i32 when computing the promise offset (which therefore
+    // shifts from 16 to 20/24).  Both sides must stay in sync.
+    (void)B.addField(Type::getInt32Ty(C), std::nullopt, /*header*/ true);
